-- ccc7-s191-offences.l4 -- sections 191 (possession of intercepting devices), 192 (forfeiture), 193 (disclosure of information), 193.1 (disclosure of radio-based telephone communications) and
-- 194 (damages) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- Offence functions answer the provision's own question: JUST TRUE (every element holds and no saving provision applies), JUST FALSE (an element is shown not to hold, or a saving provision applies), NOTHING (a term is not covered).
-- JUST FALSE is NOT a finding of innocence. A saving limb answers JUST TRUE when its facts hold, JUST FALSE when its own conditions fail (marginal reading (a)), NOTHING when a borrowed term is not covered.
-- Grants named "may" whose "if" gate fails answer NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); "may ... where" grants answer JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) and are listed for a lawyer (F11).

§ `Section 191 -- Possession, etc.`

-- 191(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to (a) a police officer in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1) in the course of his employment; (b) a person in possession of such a device or component for the purpose of
-- using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with an authorization; (b.1) a person in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties
-- as a police officer; (c) an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member, as the case may be;
-- and (d) any other person in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness."
-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3979 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:3980 | (a) a police officer in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1) in the course of his employment;
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2)(a) (src:3978-3980)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer, by s 183 police officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possession is in the course of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2)(a) a police officer is in possession in the course of employment` MEANS
    IF `the person is a police officer, by s 183 police officer` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a "police officer" is for section 183 and is not covered
    ELSE IF (`the person is a police officer, by s 183 police officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1)` AND `the possession is in the course of his employment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a police officer in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1) in the course of his employment"

-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3981 | (b) a person in possession of such a device or component for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with an authorization;
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2)(b) (src:3978-3981)
GIVEN `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is in possession for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2)(b) a person is in possession to use it in an interception in accordance with an authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is in possession for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with that instrument`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person in possession of such a device or component for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with an authorization"
        IF `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with an authorization"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instrument is an "authorization" is for section 183 and is not covered

-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3982 | (b.1) a person in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties as a police officer;
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2)(b.1) (src:3978-3982)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties as a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2)(b.1) a person is in possession under the direction of a police officer to assist that officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties as a police officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties as a police officer"

-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3983 | (c) an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member, as the case may be; and
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2)(c) (src:3978-3983)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2)(c) an officer, servant or member of the Canadian Forces is in possession in the course of duties` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces` AND `the person is in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member, as the case may be"

-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3984 | (d) any other person in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2)(d) (src:3978-3984)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2)(d) a person is in possession under the authority of a licence` MEANS
    IF `the person is in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other person in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness"

-- 191(2) as a whole: "Subsection (1) does not apply to" a person within any of (a) to (d). FORK (F14): "(c) ...; and (d)" is read as a list of exempted persons (a union), not as requirements on one person.
-- src:3978 | Exemptions
-- src:3979 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:3980 | (a) a police officer in possession of a device or component described in subsection (1) in the course of his employment;
-- src:3981 | (b) a person in possession of such a device or component for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with an authorization;
-- src:3982 | (b.1) a person in possession of such a device or component under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of his duties as a police officer;
-- src:3983 | (c) an officer or a servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces in possession of such a device or component in the course of his duties as such an officer, servant or member, as the case may be; and
-- src:3984 | (d) any other person in possession of such a device or component under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(2) (src:3978-3984)
GIVEN `s 191(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 191(2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 191(2)(b.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 191(2)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 191(2)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on a term that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `s 191(2)(a)` , `s 191(2)(b)` , `s 191(2)(b.1)` , `s 191(2)(c)` , `s 191(2)(d)`)

-- 191(1): "Every person who possesses, sells or purchases any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device or any component of it knowing that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications
-- is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:3974 | Possession, etc.
-- src:3975 | 191 (1) Every person who possesses, sells or purchases any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device or any component of it knowing that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications is guilty of
-- src:3976 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3977 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(1) (src:3974-3977)
GIVEN `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did is selling, by s 183 sell` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person purchases it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a component of such a device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 191(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 191(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who possesses, sells or purchases any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device or any component of it knowing that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications is guilty of"
        IF (`the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 191(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): an element or the saving provision turns on a term that is not covered (an act "sell includes" does not name, or a borrowed term)
    WHERE
        `the elements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `s 183 three-valued any of`
                        (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person possesses it`
                            , `what the person did is selling, by s 183 sell`
                            , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person purchases it`)
                    , `s 183 three-valued any of`
                        (LIST `the thing is an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
                            , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the thing is a component of such a device`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person knows that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications`)

-- src:3976 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
@ref Criminal Code s 191(1)(a) (src:3976-3976)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 191(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`
                    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
                    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:3977 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(1)(b) (src:3977-3977)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 191(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3974 | Possession, etc.
-- src:3975 | 191 (1) Every person who possesses, sells or purchases any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device or any component of it knowing that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications is guilty of
-- src:3976 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3977 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(1) (src:3974-3977)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 191(1) the punishments` MEANS
    LIST `s 191(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`
        , `s 191(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3974 | Possession, etc.
-- src:3975 | 191 (1) Every person who possesses, sells or purchases any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device or any component of it knowing that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications is guilty of
-- src:3976 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3977 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(1) (src:3974-3977)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 191(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 191(3): "A licence issued for the purpose of paragraph (2)(d) may contain such terms and conditions relating to the possession, sale or purchase of a device or component described in subsection (1) as the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness may prescribe."
-- src:3985 | Terms and conditions of licence
-- src:3986 | (3) A licence issued for the purpose of paragraph (2)(d) may contain such terms and conditions relating to the possession, sale or purchase of a device or component described in subsection (1) as the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness may prescribe.
@ref Criminal Code s 191(3) (src:3985-3986)
GIVEN `the licence was issued for the purpose of paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term relates to the possession, sale or purchase of a device or component described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness prescribes it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 191(3) the licence may contain the term` MEANS
    IF `the licence was issued for the purpose of paragraph (2)(d)` AND `the term relates to the possession, sale or purchase of a device or component described in subsection (1)` AND `the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness prescribes it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such terms and conditions relating to the possession, sale or purchase of a device or component described in subsection (1) as the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness may prescribe"

§ `Section 192 -- Forfeiture`

-- 192(1): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191, any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence, on the conviction,
-- in addition to any punishment that is imposed, may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty whereupon it may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs." A "may ... where" grant: a failed "Where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (F11).
-- src:3987 | Forfeiture
-- src:3988 | 192 (1) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191, any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence, on the conviction, in addition to any punishment that is imposed, may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty whereupon it may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 192(1) (src:3987-3988)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is one by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(1) the device may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191"
        IF `the device is one by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence"

-- src:3987 | Forfeiture
-- src:3988 | 192 (1) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191, any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device by means of which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence, on the conviction, in addition to any punishment that is imposed, may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty whereupon it may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 192(1) (src:3987-3988)
GIVEN `the device has been ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(1) the forfeited device may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs` MEANS
    IF `the device has been ordered forfeited to Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whereupon it may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs"

-- 192(2): "No order for forfeiture shall be made under subsection (1) in respect of telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to
-- the public or forming part of the telephone, telegraph or other communication service or system of that person by means of which an offence under section 184 has been committed if that person was not a party to the offence."
-- Named for the bar: JUST TRUE = no order for forfeiture shall be made; JUST FALSE = the provider was a party ("if that person was not a party"); NOTHING = not a facility the bar speaks to.
-- src:3989 | Limitation
-- src:3990 | (2) No order for forfeiture shall be made under subsection (1) in respect of telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public or forming part of the telephone, telegraph or other communication service or system of that person by means of which an offence under section 184 has been committed if that person was not a party to the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 192(2) (src:3989-3990)
GIVEN `the thing is communication facilities or equipment owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public, or forming part of the service or system of that person, by means of which an offence under section 184 has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person was a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 192(2) no order for forfeiture shall be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing is communication facilities or equipment owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public, or forming part of the service or system of that person, by means of which an offence under section 184 has been committed`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public"
        IF `that person was a party to the offence`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person was not a party to the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 193 -- Disclosure of information`

-- 193(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication or any part thereof or the substance, meaning or purport thereof or of any part thereof or who discloses the existence of a private communication
-- (a) in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath;"
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4000 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication or any part thereof or the substance, meaning or purport thereof or of any part thereof or who discloses the existence of a private communication
-- src:4001 | (a) in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath;
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(a) (src:3999-4001)
GIVEN `the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(a) the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath"

-- (b) in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation if the private communication was lawfully intercepted;
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4002 | (b) in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation if the private communication was lawfully intercepted;
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(b) (src:3999-4002)
GIVEN `the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(b) the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation` AND `the private communication was lawfully intercepted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation if the private communication was lawfully intercepted"

-- (c) in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190;
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4003 | (c) in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190;
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(c) (src:3999-4003)
GIVEN `the disclosure is in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(c) the disclosure is in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190"

-- (d) in the course of the operation of (i) a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public, (ii) a department or an agency of the Government of Canada, or (iii) services relating to the management or protection of a computer system,
-- as defined in subsection 342.1(2), if the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e);
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4004 | (d) in the course of the operation of
-- src:4005 | (i) a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public,
-- src:4006 | (ii) a department or an agency of the Government of Canada, or
-- src:4007 | (iii) services relating to the management or protection of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2),
-- src:4008 | if the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e);
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(d) (src:3999-4008)
GIVEN `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of a department or an agency of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(d) the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)"
        IF `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` OR `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of a department or an agency of the Government of Canada`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the disclosure is in the course of the operation of services relating to the management or protection of a computer system`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the course of the operation of"
        IF `the thing is a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the thing is a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "services relating to the management or protection of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a "computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)" is for that subsection and is not covered

-- (e) where disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences and is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere;
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4009 | (e) where disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences and is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere; or
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(e) (src:3999-4009)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(e) the disclosure is made to a peace officer, prosecutor or foreign authority in the interests of the administration of justice` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences` AND `it is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences and is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere"

-- (f) where the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act.
-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4010 | (f) where the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2)(f) (src:3999-4010)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2)(f) the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service` AND `it is for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act"

-- src:3999 | Exemptions
-- src:4000 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication or any part thereof or the substance, meaning or purport thereof or of any part thereof or who discloses the existence of a private communication
-- src:4001 | (a) in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or in any other proceedings in which the person may be required to give evidence on oath;
-- src:4002 | (b) in the course of or for the purpose of any criminal investigation if the private communication was lawfully intercepted;
-- src:4003 | (c) in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars pursuant to an order under section 190;
-- src:4004 | (d) in the course of the operation of
-- src:4005 | (i) a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public,
-- src:4006 | (ii) a department or an agency of the Government of Canada, or
-- src:4007 | (iii) services relating to the management or protection of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2),
-- src:4008 | if the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e);
-- src:4009 | (e) where disclosure is made to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a person or authority with responsibility in a foreign state for the investigation or prosecution of offences and is intended to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere; or
-- src:4010 | (f) where the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or to an employee of the Service for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(2) (src:3999-4010)
GIVEN `s 193(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 193(2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 193(2)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 193(2)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 193(2)(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 193(2)(f)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on a term that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `s 193(2)(a)` , `s 193(2)(b)` , `s 193(2)(c)` , `s 193(2)(d)` , `s 193(2)(e)` , `s 193(2)(f)`)

-- 193(3): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication or any part thereof or the substance, meaning or purport thereof or of any part thereof or who discloses the existence of a private communication where that which is
-- disclosed by him was, prior to the disclosure, lawfully disclosed in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings referred to in paragraph (2)(a)."
-- src:4011 | Publishing of prior lawful disclosure
-- src:4012 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication or any part thereof or the substance, meaning or purport thereof or of any part thereof or who discloses the existence of a private communication where that which is disclosed by him was, prior to the disclosure, lawfully disclosed in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings referred to in paragraph (2)(a).
@ref Criminal Code s 193(3) (src:4011-4012)
GIVEN `that which is disclosed by the person was, prior to the disclosure, lawfully disclosed in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(3) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses what was already lawfully disclosed in evidence` MEANS
    IF `that which is disclosed by the person was, prior to the disclosure, lawfully disclosed in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings referred to in paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that which is disclosed by him was, prior to the disclosure, lawfully disclosed in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings referred to in paragraph (2)(a)"

-- 193(1): "If a private communication has been intercepted by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator of that communication or of the person intended by the originator
-- to receive it, every person commits an offence who, without the express consent of the originator of that communication or of the person intended to receive it, knowingly (a) uses or discloses the private communication or any part of it or the substance,
-- meaning or purpose of it or of any part of it, or (b) discloses the existence of the private communication." The offence's own "If" clause is part of the question: where it fails the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3991 | Disclosure of information
-- src:3992 | 193 (1) If a private communication has been intercepted by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator of that communication or of the person intended by the originator to receive it, every person commits an offence who, without the express consent of the originator of that communication or of the person intended to receive it, knowingly
-- src:3993 | (a) uses or discloses the private communication or any part of it or the substance, meaning or purpose of it or of any part of it, or
-- src:3994 | (b) discloses the existence of the private communication.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(1) (src:3991-3994)
GIVEN `the communication is a private communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was intercepted by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interception was without the consent, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended by the originator to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without the express consent of the originator or of the person intended to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses or discloses the private communication or any part of it or the substance, meaning or purpose of it or of any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses the existence of the private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 193(2) or (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193(1) the person commits an offence under the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 193(2) or (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses a private communication"
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who, without the express consent of the originator of that communication or of the person intended to receive it, knowingly"
        IF (`the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 193(2) or (3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an element or the saving provision turns on a term that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the elements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `the communication is a private communication, by s 183`
                    , `it was intercepted by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the interception was without the consent, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended by the originator to receive it`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acted without the express consent of the originator or of the person intended to receive it`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acted knowingly`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (`the person uses or discloses the private communication or any part of it or the substance, meaning or purpose of it or of any part of it` OR `the person discloses the existence of the private communication`))

-- 193(1.1): "Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:3996 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:3997 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
@ref Criminal Code s 193(1.1)(a) (src:3996-3997)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 193(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`
                    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
                    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:3998 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(1.1)(b) (src:3998-3998)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 193(1.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3995 | Punishment
-- src:3996 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:3997 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3998 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(1.1) (src:3995-3998)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 193(1.1) the punishments` MEANS
    LIST `s 193(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment`
        , `s 193(1.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3995 | Punishment
-- src:3996 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:3997 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3998 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 193(1.1) (src:3995-3998)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 193(1.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 193.1 -- Disclosure of information received from interception of radio-based telephone communications`

-- 193.1(1): "Every person who knowingly uses or discloses a radio-based telephone communication or who knowingly discloses the existence of such a communication is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than
-- two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, if (a) the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it was in Canada when the communication was made; (b) the
-- communication was intercepted by means of an electromagnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator ... or the person intended ...; and (c) the person does not have the express or implied consent
-- of the originator ... or the person intended ...". Subsection (2) brings 193(2) and (3) to this offence: their combined answer, as they apply here, is an input.
-- src:4013 | Disclosure of information received from interception of radio-based telephone communications
-- src:4014 | 193.1 (1) Every person who knowingly uses or discloses a radio-based telephone communication or who knowingly discloses the existence of such a communication is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, if
-- src:4015 | (a) the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it was in Canada when the communication was made;
-- src:4016 | (b) the communication was intercepted by means of an electromagnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator of the communication or of the person intended by the originator to receive the communication; and
-- src:4017 | (c) the person does not have the express or implied consent of the originator of the communication or of the person intended by the originator to receive the communication.
@ref Criminal Code s 193.1(1) (src:4013-4017)
GIVEN `the communication is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person uses or discloses it, or discloses its existence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it was in Canada when the communication was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was intercepted by means of an electromagnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not have the express or implied consent of the originator or of the person intended to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections 193(2) and (3) exempt the person, as they apply by s 193.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193.1(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsections 193(2) and (3) exempt the person, as they apply by s 193.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections 193(2) and (3) apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to disclosures of radio-based telephone communications"
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who knowingly uses or discloses a radio-based telephone communication or who knowingly discloses the existence of such a communication is guilty of"
        IF (`the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsections 193(2) and (3) exempt the person, as they apply by s 193.1(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an element or the saving provision turns on a term that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the elements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `the communication is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person uses or discloses it, or discloses its existence`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acted knowingly`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it was in Canada when the communication was made`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was intercepted by means of an electromagnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the consent, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended to receive it`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person does not have the express or implied consent of the originator or of the person intended to receive it`)

-- src:4014 | 193.1 (1) Every person who knowingly uses or discloses a radio-based telephone communication or who knowingly discloses the existence of such a communication is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, if
@ref Criminal Code s 193.1(1)(a) (src:4014-4014)
