§ `Section 194 -- Damages`

-- 194(2): "No amount shall be ordered to be paid under subsection (1) to a person who has commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act." Named for the bar: JUST TRUE = no amount shall be ordered.
-- src:4022 | No damages where civil proceedings commenced
-- src:4023 | (2) No amount shall be ordered to be paid under subsection (1) to a person who has commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 194(2) (src:4022-4023)
GIVEN `the person has commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(2) no amount shall be ordered to be paid to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who has commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act"

-- 194(1): "Subject to subsection (2), a court that convicts an accused of an offence under section 184, 184.5, 193 or 193.1 may, on the application of a person aggrieved, at the time sentence is imposed, order the accused to pay to that person an amount
-- not exceeding five thousand dollars as punitive damages." A grant ("may") limited by its own wording (the offences, the application, the time, the amount): outside the limit it is NOT COVERED; "Subject to subsection (2)" is the saving input.
-- src:4020 | Damages
-- src:4021 | 194 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a court that convicts an accused of an offence under section 184, 184.5, 193 or 193.1 may, on the application of a person aggrieved, at the time sentence is imposed, order the accused to pay to that person an amount not exceeding five thousand dollars as punitive damages.
@ref Criminal Code s 194(1) (src:4020-4021)
GIVEN `the offence of which the accused is convicted` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the order is made on the application of a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made at the time sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the court orders the accused to pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 194(2) no amount shall be ordered to be paid to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(1) the court may order the accused to pay punitive damages to the person aggrieved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 194(2) no amount shall be ordered to be paid to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF (`the offence of which the accused is convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 184 OR `the offence of which the accused is convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 184.5 OR `the offence of which the accused is convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 193 OR `the offence of which the accused is convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 193.1)
           AND `the order is made on the application of a person aggrieved`
           AND `the order is made at the time sentence is imposed`
           AND (`the amount the court orders the accused to pay, in dollars` AT MOST 5000)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an amount not exceeding five thousand dollars as punitive damages"

-- The most the court may order under 194(1): "an amount not exceeding five thousand dollars" (dollars).
-- src:4020 | Damages
-- src:4021 | 194 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a court that convicts an accused of an offence under section 184, 184.5, 193 or 193.1 may, on the application of a person aggrieved, at the time sentence is imposed, order the accused to pay to that person an amount not exceeding five thousand dollars as punitive damages.
@ref Criminal Code s 194(1) (src:4020-4021)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 194(1) the most that may be ordered as punitive damages, in dollars` MEANS 5000

-- 194(3): "Where an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith, the applicant may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment, in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held, the amount ordered to be paid,
-- and that judgment is enforceable against the accused in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the accused in that court in civil proceedings." A "may ... where" grant: a failed "Where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (F11).
-- src:4024 | Judgment may be registered
-- src:4025 | (3) Where an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith, the applicant may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment, in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held, the amount ordered to be paid, and that judgment is enforceable against the accused in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the accused in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref Criminal Code s 194(3) (src:4024-4025)
GIVEN `an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is filed in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(3) the applicant may enter the order as a judgment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith"
        IF `the order is filed in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by filing the order, enter as a judgment, in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held"

-- src:4024 | Judgment may be registered
-- src:4025 | (3) Where an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) is not paid forthwith, the applicant may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment, in the superior court of the province in which the trial was held, the amount ordered to be paid, and that judgment is enforceable against the accused in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the accused in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref Criminal Code s 194(3) (src:4024-4025)
GIVEN `the order has been entered as a judgment under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 194(3) the judgment is enforceable against the accused as a civil judgment of the court` MEANS
    IF `the order has been entered as a judgment under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that judgment is enforceable against the accused in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the accused in that court in civil proceedings"

-- 194(4): "All or any part of an amount that is ordered to be paid under subsection (1) may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the accused at the time of his arrest, except where there is a dispute respecting ownership of or right of
-- possession to those moneys by claimants other than the accused." JUST FALSE where there is such a dispute ("except where").
